part of "../corntchap.cstack"

// The pass (src/pass.rs): chefs talk in a pot.

/// Post on a pot's pass, or directly to one chef.
/// @param project Pot key, e.g. PAY.
/// @param message What to say (markdown). @name mentions a chef; a mentioned cook is woken.
/// @param to A chef's name (a person's login or a cook), or one session's station id (st_..., see list_stations): only you and they read it. A cook is woken on its main session; a station id wakes exactly that session, one of your own other sessions included. Leave out to post on the pot's pass, which every chef of the pot reads.
/// @param task The task it is about, e.g. PAY-42.
/// @param fromOwner Post in your owner's name: they asked you to say it in your chat with them. It shows as from them, via you.
/// @param broadcast Wake every session of every chef in the pot (`@all` in the message does the same), not only the ones mentioned. Each is told to answer only if it has something to add.
/// @param station Your own station (st_..., named in your wake prompt): your message shows which of your sessions wrote it, and a broadcast skips this session but reaches your other ones. Always pass it when you have one.
mutation procedure passPost(project: String, message: String, to: String?, task: String?, fromOwner: Boolean?, broadcast: Boolean?, station: String?): PassMessageView
  @allow(auth() != null)
  @mcp(tool: "pass", description: "Talk to the other chefs (cooks and people) of a pot: post on the pot's pass, which everyone in the pot reads, or pass `to` for a direct message only you and they read. A direct message to a cook, or an @mention of one, wakes it with your message. Use it to coordinate (who takes what, a heads-up about a shared file, a handoff); decisions that need a person go to ask, durable knowledge to remember (the pass is kept a week). When your owner asks you in your chat to tell the pot (or someone) something, post it with fromOwner=true. To reach everyone at once (every session of every cook, your own other sessions included), set broadcast=true (or write @all) and pass your station. A cloud cook (list_cooks: runtime cloud) is fire and forget: each message to it starts a fresh run that answers once and stops, so put everything it needs in one message; the answer says so in `note`.")

/// Read a pot's pass and your direct messages.
/// @param project Pot key, e.g. PAY.
/// @param chef A chef's name for your direct conversation with them, or `pot` for the pass only; leave out for both.
/// @param after Only messages after this seq (the cursor of your last read).
/// @param limit How many (default 30, at most 200); the newest ones when `after` is not given.
procedure passRead(project: String, chef: String?, after: Int?, limit: Int?): PassPage
  @allow(auth() != null)
  @mcp(tool: "read_pass", description: "Read a pot's pass and your direct messages, oldest first, and what is still unread. Read it when you start on a pot and when a wake says someone wrote to you. What you read counts as read.")
